1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,340
In my family, when the phone rings after 10, somebody

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:08,400
is sitting in a room with a table, two chairs, and a man

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,670
telling them this is their only chance.

4
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:14,170
I know that room. I sat in it at 17.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:17,540
Nobody asked me what happened, not the police, not the

6
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:20,450
prosecutor, not even the lawyer I paid.

7
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:22,830
Nobody asked what happened.

8
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:29,260
Let me tell you where we're from first, because nobody

9
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,250
in those rooms ever did.

10
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:36,200
On our block, you learn the sound of gunshots before you

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,670
learn your times tables.

12
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,410
Cars slow down for no reason.

13
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:42,730
Somebody's cousin didn't make it home.

14
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:47,150
Last summer, the police take 40 minutes if they come.

15
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,570
So people get protection however they can.

16
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:54,280
From a friend, from a friend of a friend, from Lord knows

17
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:58,550
who, nobody's thinking about paperwork.

18
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:02,450
They're thinking about getting home alive.

19
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,640
When the danger is that close, being safe matters more

20
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:10,980
than being legal. And a lot of people in danger aren't

21
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:13,110
even old enough to be legal yet.

22
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,920
That's not an excuse.

23
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:18,490
It's the truth. Nobody puts in the report.

24
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:22,530
The Bible has a word for people like us, the oppressed.

25
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:26,500
Under-protected when we call for help, over watched when

26
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,650
we're just standing outside, over punished when we slip,

27
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:33,120
and with no opportunities to get out from under any of

28
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:36,480
it. The police don't come when we need them, but they

29
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:40,700
come for us. It started under a picture online, two girls

30
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,950
I barely knew decided I was the problem.

31
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:45,700
Comments turned into messages, messages turned into I

32
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:46,890
know where you stay.

33
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,480
Then came a house party.

34
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,940
I didn't go looking for them.

35
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:51,370
They came looking for me.

36
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:52,960
Both of them were 19.

37
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,330
I was 17. The first one swung.

38
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:58,110
The bottle was already in my hand.

39
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,900
When it was over, her tooth was gone, and I was the one

40
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:05,770
the police wanted. They didn't find me on their own.

41
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:09,650
The girls gave them my relatives' information.

42
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:13,030
Jada. Jada went to school with them.

43
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:16,480
Her mother got on the phone and made her give the police

44
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,510
my name and where I lived.

45
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:23,670
Jada and I haven't talked since.

46
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:28,850
One phone call can change who your family is to you.

47
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,890
The report said I hit her with a bottle.

48
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:35,400
That was true. It didn't say she came at me first.

49
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:37,180
It didn't say there were two of them.

50
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:40,010
Felonious assault, one night in jail.

51
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,460
I didn't wait for a public defender.

52
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:48,070
I paid for a lawyer myself.

53
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:58,900
Me, 17 years old, 1 ,600 up front, and the remainder of

54
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:03,110
10 ,000. Every dollar I worked for it.

55
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:07,180
I met him for maybe 10 minutes at a time.

56
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:11,980
Twice. Always and past that.

57
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:14,800
He had a stack of folders under his arms and a suit on

58
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,210
with a white shirt and a red tie.

59
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:23,160
Usually, blue or gray pants, and my folder was just one

60
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:26,180
of them. He never asked me what happened, not once.

61
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:30,840
He never asked about the messages or that there were two

62
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,080
of them or who swung first.

63
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:38,200
It's quite odd because he read the reports from the both

64
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:41,250
of them, and that didn't trigger in his mind.

65
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:45,860
I'm looking at the date of birth and the reports that

66
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:47,010
I have been jumped.

67
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:52,610
All he said is... There's a youth program.

68
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:56,120
Play it, finish your probation, and it comes off your

69
00:03:56,120 --> 00:04:01,920
record. Fight it. You're betting your whole life on a

70
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:05,360
jury? I paid him like a private lawyer, and he treated

71
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:08,650
me like one more name on the list.

72
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,380
Paid or free, it felt the same.

73
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:13,850
The deal was already decided before he ever met me.

74
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:20,900
So I pled. Two years of probation, a restraining order,

75
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,080
close to $10 ,000 in all opportunity.

76
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,850
He handled the restitution and the fees.

77
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,500
Before all of this, I was on honor row.

78
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,450
I didn't drink. I didn't do drugs.

79
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:32,930
I was the girl teachers didn't worry about.

80
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:36,820
After, I was a 17 -year -old paying off a criminal case,

81
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:40,010
lawyer payments, restitution, court costs, probation fees,

82
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:43,410
anger management classes, I paid for myself.

83
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:46,020
The no contact order and the charges on my record kept

84
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:47,240
me out of regular jobs.

85
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,640
Nobody with an application in the background check would

86
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:53,120
take me. So I took whatever worked with payment, and I

87
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:55,570
took all of it I could get.

88
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:56,800
I went to school tired.

89
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:01,370
When I went at all, I left with a 1 .5, I barely graduated.

90
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,590
That's what the deal cost.

91
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,430
Not just the money.

92
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:08,240
The girl I was going to be.

93
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,530
The record clear, I didn't.

94
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:15,340
For years, I walked into every room expecting someone

95
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:26,610
to point at me. Now, my cousin Tasha is the strong one.

96
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,280
She works doubles, pays her own way.

97
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,720
She lives on the street where two houses got shot at the

98
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:35,860
summer before. She didn't have a license for a gun in

99
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:39,320
her purse. She had it because she was tired of being afraid

100
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:40,990
to walk to her car.

101
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:53,930
At a party, her boyfriend got jumped.

102
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,700
Three men had him on the ground.

103
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,140
Kicking his head, she screamed.

104
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:01,630
Nobody stopped. Six shots.

105
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:05,940
One hit a man who was stomping him, and one hit the man

106
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:07,330
she was trying to save.

107
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,500
I told them, they were killing him.

108
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,790
They said, Then why'd you keep shooting?

109
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:14,980
Then they asked where I got the gun, and that's all they

110
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,590
wanted to talk about.

111
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,650
Her lawyer had her case and about a hundred others.

112
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:24,240
He told her that without a license, self -defense was

113
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:30,720
a hard sell. He told her what 20 years sounds like, and

114
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,260
here's what scared her the most.

115
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:35,460
She didn't know where that gun had really been.

116
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:38,370
She bought it off somebody who knew somebody.

117
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,540
Was the serial number clean?

118
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:44,480
Was it stolen? Had it been used or something before it

119
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:46,530
ever got to her? Nobody knew.

120
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:51,450
None of that was in the discovery.

121
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:54,270
So the prosecutor was holding a blank check.

122
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:57,500
Any day a lab report could come back and turn one charge

123
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:01,140
into five. Fighting meant betting on a gun whose history

124
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:04,850
she couldn't see. I told her, say it was self -defense.

125
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,970
Say it out loud. Make them answer it.

126
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:11,110
But she was scared, and who wouldn't be?

127
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:15,790
I took the plea. I just wanted to come home.

128
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:19,860
She came home with a record and a question she'll carry

129
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:23,130
forever. What if I had said it?

130
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,390
Now Marcus is the baby.

131
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:33,830
Sixteen, seventeen soon.

132
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,850
He plays the video games with my son.

133
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,610
Two boys from his school got shot that year.

134
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,010
He stopped taking the bus.

135
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:47,900
Too young to carry legally, but old enough to be scared

136
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:52,940
to death. The police came with a warrant at six in the

137
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:58,500
morning and found a gun in bed with him that wasn't registered

138
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:06,860
to anybody. Just tell me it's yours and this all goes

139
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:12,060
away? No parent in the room, no lawyer yet, a sixteen

140
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:16,010
-year -old who wanted to be over, he said it was his.

141
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:20,460
By the time his lawyer met him, that one sentence was

142
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:24,740
the whole case. Nobody asked him why a sixteen -year -old

143
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:27,870
fell. He needed a gun just to get to school.

144
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:31,620
No contest. He was sent to placement two hours from his

145
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:34,480
home. His lawyer couldn't tell the family where the gun

146
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:38,440
came from either. No trace report, no serial number history,

147
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,340
nothing in the script.

148
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:41,620
Just a warning that if it came back tied to something

149
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:43,210
else, it would all get worse.

150
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:47,160
A boy and his grandmother asked to bet against a blank

151
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:50,830
page. They didn't even let him sit.

152
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:56,340
I'm not saying none of us did anything.

153
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,680
Guns without papers are still against the law and I didn't

154
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:01,270
want one more child carrying one.

155
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:05,940
I'm saying nobody asked what happened or why before they

156
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:07,230
offered us the deal.

157
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,710
So here's what I teach my children now.

158
00:09:09,780 --> 00:09:12,980
You can stay silent, say I want a lawyer, and then stop

159
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:16,790
talking. If you're under eighteen, ask for your parent.

160
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:19,820
If you were defending yourself or anyone else, tell your

161
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:23,260
lawyer everything. Whether your lawyer is paid or free,

162
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:27,330
they work for you. Ask them, have you heard my whole side?

163
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:31,310
And if they haven't, make them sit down and listen.

164
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:33,810
Write it out and hand it to them.

165
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:36,330
Don't sign anything you don't understand.

166
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:40,750
Ask what it will do to your life in ten years.

167
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,760
Before you take any deal, ask your lawyer.

168
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:45,740
Have we seen all the evidence including the gun tracing

169
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:49,470
and lab reports? Defend the poor and fatherless.

170
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:52,210
Do justice to the afflicted and needy.

171
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:58,020
Psalm 82 verse 3 The Lord executes righteousness and judgment

172
00:09:58,020 --> 00:10:00,210
for all that are oppressed.

173
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:05,480
Psalm 103 verse 6 The Lord also will be a refuge for the

174
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:09,270
oppressed. A refuge in times of trouble.

175
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:13,220
Psalm 9 verse 9 The Lord sees the room with the table

176
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,220
and the two chairs.

177
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:16,560
He sees the street where you live and He sees who was

178
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:20,160
never asked. Did your lawyer ever ask you what really

179
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:22,310
happened? Tell me in the comments.

